IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc17-journalists.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 488.01 and 488.02: applications for warrants, authorizations and orders that relate to a journalist's
-- communications or sources, and the sealed documents obtained. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Same conventions as ccc17-dna-orders.l4.
-- The definitions of "data", "document", "journalist" and "journalistic source" point at section 487.011 (another part) and at the Canada Evidence Act (not among the sources):
-- the first two are seam inputs (`s 487.011 ...`, MAYBE BOOLEAN), the others are asked as facts about the person; a "no" to a fact asked about another Act is NOTHING, not the text's no.

§ `Section 488.01 -- Journalists: definitions`

-- covers: 488.01(1) "data"
-- jural: none
-- src:9865 | data has the same meaning as in section 487.011. (données)
@ref s 488.01(1) "data" (src:9865)
GIVEN `s 487.011 data: the thing is data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(1) data` MEANS `s 487.011 data: the thing is data`   -- "has the same meaning as in section 487.011": the answer of that section, carried through (JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE; NOTHING when section 487.011 is itself not covered)

-- covers: 488.01(1) "document"
-- jural: none
-- src:9866 | document has the same meaning as in section 487.011. (document)
@ref s 488.01(1) "document" (src:9866)
GIVEN `s 487.011 document: the thing is a document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(1) document` MEANS `s 487.011 document: the thing is a document`   -- "has the same meaning as in section 487.011": the answer of that section, carried through

-- covers: 488.01(1) "journalist"
-- jural: none
-- src:9867 | journalist has the same meaning as in subsection 39.1(1) of the Canada Evidence Act. (journaliste)
@ref s 488.01(1) "journalist" (src:9867)
GIVEN `the person is a journalist within the meaning of subsection 39.1(1) of the Canada Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(1) journalist` MEANS
    IF `the person is a journalist within the meaning of subsection 39.1(1) of the Canada Evidence Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- covers: 488.01(1) "journalistic source"
-- jural: none
-- src:9868 | journalistic source has the same meaning as in subsection 39.1(1) of the Canada Evidence Act. (source journalistique)
@ref s 488.01(1) "journalistic source" (src:9868)
GIVEN `the person is a journalistic source within the meaning of subsection 39.1(1) of the Canada Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(1) journalistic source` MEANS
    IF `the person is a journalistic source within the meaning of subsection 39.1(1) of the Canada Evidence Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- covers: 488.01(1) "officer"
-- jural: none
-- src:9869 | officer means a peace officer or public officer. (fonctionnaire)
@ref s 488.01(1) "officer" (src:9869)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 public officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(1) officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 2 public officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 2 public officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "officer means a peace officer or public officer"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

§ `Section 488.01 -- Journalists: the application, the judge and the conditions`

-- covers: 488.01(1)
-- jural: none
-- src:9864 | 488.01 (1) The following definitions apply in this section and in section 488.02.
@ref s 488.01(1) (lead-in) (src:9864)
-- The definitions of subsection (1) apply "in this section and in section 488.02" (the five functions above).
`s 488.01(1) the definitions apply in this section and in section 488.02` MEANS TRUE

-- covers: 488.01(2)
-- jural: a journalist > an applicant for a warrant, authorization or order > immunity
-- src:9871 | (2) Despite any other provision of this Act, if an applicant for a warrant under section 487.01, 492.1 or 492.2, a search warrant under this Act, notably under section 487, an authorization under section 184.2, 186 or 188, or an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 knows that the application relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist, they shall make the application to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or to a judge as defined in section 552. That judge has exclusive jurisdiction to dispose of the application.
@ref s 488.01(2) (src:9871)
-- The instruments named: warrants under section 487.01, 492.1 or 492.2; a search warrant under this Act, notably under section 487; an authorization under section 184.2, 186 or 188; an order under any of
-- sections 487.014 to 487.017. "notably" and the list make it a list not closed with "only": another instrument is NOTHING. The knowledge gate is the text's own "if": a duty, so JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `the applicant knows that the application relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section number of the instrument` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a search warrant under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(2) the applicant shall make the application to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the applicant knows that the application relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an applicant for a warrant under section 487.01, 492.1 or 492.2, a search warrant under this Act, notably under section 487, an authorization under section 184.2, 186 or 188, or an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 knows that the application relates to a journalist’s communications"
        IF `it is a search warrant under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF elem `the section number of the instrument` `s 488.01(2) the sections named` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the section number of the instrument` AT LEAST 487.014 AND `the section number of the instrument` AT MOST 487.017 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)

-- The single sections named in subsection (2): 487.01, 492.1, 492.2 (warrants) and 184.2, 186, 188 (authorizations); 487.014 to 487.017 (orders) is a range, tested in the function.
@ref s 488.01(2) (the sections named) (src:9871)
`s 488.01(2) the sections named` MEANS LIST 487.01, 492.1, 492.2, 184.2, 186, 188

@ref s 488.01(2) (exclusive jurisdiction) (src:9871)
GIVEN `the application is one that subsection (2) requires to be made to that judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(2) the judge has exclusive jurisdiction to dispose of the application` MEANS
    IF `the application is one that subsection (2) requires to be made to that judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.01(3), 488.01(3)(a), 488.01(3)(b)
-- jural: a journalist > the judge > immunity
-- src:9873 | (3) A judge may issue a warrant, authorization or order under subsection (2) only if, in addition to the conditions required for the issue of the warrant, authorization or order, he or she is satisfied that
-- src:9874 | (a) there is no other way by which the information can reasonably be obtained; and
-- src:9875 | (b) the public interest in the investigation and prosecution of a criminal offence outweighs the journalist’s right to privacy in gathering and disseminating information.
@ref s 488.01(3) (src:9873-9875)
-- "may issue ... only if, in addition to the conditions required for the issue ..., he or she is satisfied that (a) ... and (b)": closed with "only if", so JUST FALSE when either fails.
GIVEN `the conditions required for the issue of the warrant, authorization or order are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there is no other way by which the information can reasonably be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the public interest in the investigation and prosecution of a criminal offence outweighs the journalist’s right to privacy in gathering and disseminating information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(3) the judge may issue the warrant, authorization or order` MEANS
    IF `the conditions required for the issue of the warrant, authorization or order are met` AND `the judge is satisfied that there is no other way by which the information can reasonably be obtained` AND `the judge is satisfied that the public interest in the investigation and prosecution of a criminal offence outweighs the journalist’s right to privacy in gathering and disseminating information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A judge may issue a warrant, authorization or order under subsection (2) only if, in addition to the conditions required for the issue of the warrant, authorization or order"

-- covers: 488.01(4)
-- jural: the judge > a journalist > power
-- src:9877 | (4) The judge to whom the application for the warrant, authorization or order is made may, in his or her discretion, request that a special advocate present observations in the interests of freedom of the press concerning the conditions set out in subsection (3).
@ref s 488.01(4) (src:9877)
GIVEN `the application for the warrant, authorization or order is made to the judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(4) the judge may request that a special advocate present observations in the interests of freedom of the press concerning the conditions set out in subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the application for the warrant, authorization or order is made to the judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.01(5)
-- jural: a journalist suspected of an offence > the judge > disability
-- src:9879 | (5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not apply in respect of an application for a warrant, authorization or order that is made in relation to the commission of an offence by a journalist.
@ref s 488.01(5) (src:9879)
GIVEN `the application is made in relation to the commission of an offence by a journalist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(5) subsections (3) and (4) do not apply` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in relation to the commission of an offence by a journalist`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- covers: 488.01(6)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: the judge > a journalist suspected of an offence > power
-- src:9881 | (6) If a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) is sought in relation to the commission of an offence by a journalist and the judge considers it necessary to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources, the judge may order that some or all documents obtained pursuant to the warrant, authorization or order are to be dealt with in accordance with section 488.02.
@ref s 488.01(6) (src:9881)
GIVEN `the warrant, authorization or order is sought in relation to the commission of an offence by a journalist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers it necessary to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(6) the judge may order that some or all documents obtained are to be dealt with in accordance with section 488.02` MEANS
    IF `the warrant, authorization or order is sought in relation to the commission of an offence by a journalist` AND `the judge considers it necessary to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.01(7)
-- jural: a journalist > the judge > right
-- src:9883 | (7) The warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) may contain any conditions that the judge considers appropriate to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities.
@ref s 488.01(7) (src:9883)
GIVEN `the judge considers the condition appropriate to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(7) the warrant, authorization or order may contain the condition` MEANS
    IF `the judge considers the condition appropriate to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.01(8)
-- jural: the judge > the applicant > power
-- src:9885 | (8) The judge who rules on the application for the warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) has the same powers, with the necessary adaptations, as the authority who may issue the warrant, authorization or order.
@ref s 488.01(8) (src:9885)
GIVEN `the judge rules on the application for the warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(8) the judge has the same powers, with the necessary adaptations, as the authority who may issue the warrant, authorization or order` MEANS
    IF `the judge rules on the application for the warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.01(9), 488.01(9)(a), 488.01(9)(b)
-- jural: a journalist > an officer > right
-- src:9887 | (9) If an officer, acting under a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) for which an application was not made in accordance with that subsection, becomes aware that the warrant, authorization or order relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist, the officer shall, as soon as possible, make an ex parte application to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 and, until the judge disposes of the application,
-- src:9888 | (a) refrain from examining or reproducing, in whole or in part, any document obtained pursuant to the warrant, authorization or order; and
-- src:9889 | (b) place any document obtained pursuant to the warrant, authorization or order in a sealed packet and keep it in a place to which the public has no access.
@ref s 488.01(9) (src:9887-9889)
GIVEN `the officer, acting under a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) for which an application was not made in accordance with that subsection, becomes aware that it relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(9) the officer shall, as soon as possible, make an ex parte application to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` MEANS
    IF `the officer, acting under a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) for which an application was not made in accordance with that subsection, becomes aware that it relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an officer, acting under a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) for which an application was not made in accordance with that subsection, becomes aware"

@ref s 488.01(9)(a) and (b) (until the judge disposes) (src:9887-9889)
GIVEN `the officer, acting under a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) for which an application was not made in accordance with that subsection, becomes aware that it relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has disposed of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(9) until the judge disposes of the application the officer shall refrain from examining or reproducing any document obtained and shall keep it in a sealed packet` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the officer, acting under a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) for which an application was not made in accordance with that subsection, becomes aware that it relates to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an officer, acting under a warrant, authorization or order referred to in subsection (2) for which an application was not made in accordance with that subsection, becomes aware"
        IF `the judge has disposed of the application` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the judge disposes of the application"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 488.01(10) order sought` IS ONE OF
    `s 488.01(10)(a) confirm the warrant, authorization or order`
    `s 488.01(10)(b) vary the warrant, authorization or order to impose conditions`
    `s 488.01(10)(c) order that some or all documents are to be dealt with in accordance with section 488.02`
    `s 488.01(10)(d) revoke the warrant, authorization or order`

-- covers: 488.01(10), 488.01(10)(a), 488.01(10)(b), 488.01(10)(c), 488.01(10)(d)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a journalist > the judge > power
-- src:9891 | (10) On an application under subsection (9), the judge may
-- src:9892 | (a) confirm the warrant, authorization or order if the judge is of the opinion that no additional conditions to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities should be imposed;
-- src:9893 | (b) vary the warrant, authorization or order to impose any conditions that the judge considers appropriate to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities;
-- src:9894 | (c) if the judge considers it necessary to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources, order that some or all documents that were or will be obtained pursuant to the warrant, authorization or order are to be dealt with in accordance with section 488.02; or
-- src:9895 | (d) revoke the warrant, authorization or order if the judge is of the opinion that the applicant knew or ought reasonably to have known that the application for the warrant, authorization or order related to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist.
@ref s 488.01(10) (src:9891-9895)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `order sought` IS A `s 488.01(10) order sought`
      `the judge is of the opinion that no additional conditions to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities should be imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers the conditions appropriate to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers it necessary to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the applicant knew or ought reasonably to have known that the application related to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.01(10) the judge may make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made under subsection (9)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `order sought` EQUALS `s 488.01(10)(a) confirm the warrant, authorization or order` AND `the judge is of the opinion that no additional conditions to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities should be imposed` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `order sought` EQUALS `s 488.01(10)(b) vary the warrant, authorization or order to impose conditions` AND `the judge considers the conditions appropriate to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources and to limit the disruption of journalistic activities` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `order sought` EQUALS `s 488.01(10)(c) order that some or all documents are to be dealt with in accordance with section 488.02` AND `the judge considers it necessary to protect the confidentiality of journalistic sources` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `order sought` EQUALS `s 488.01(10)(d) revoke the warrant, authorization or order` AND `the judge is of the opinion that the applicant knew or ought reasonably to have known that the application related to a journalist’s communications or an object, document or data relating to or in the possession of a journalist` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§ `Section 488.02 -- Journalists: documents`

-- covers: 488.02(1)
-- jural: a journalist > the court > right
-- src:9897 | 488.02 (1) Any document obtained pursuant to a warrant, authorization or order issued in accordance with subsection 488.01(3), or that is the subject of an order made under subsection 488.01(6) or paragraph 488.01(10)(c), is to be placed in a packet and sealed by the court that issued the warrant, authorization or order and is to be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in such other place as the judge may authorize and is not to be dealt with except in accordance with this section.
@ref s 488.02(1) (src:9897)
GIVEN `the document was obtained pursuant to a warrant, authorization or order issued in accordance with subsection 488.01(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is the subject of an order made under subsection 488.01(6) or paragraph 488.01(10)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.02(1) the document shall be placed in a packet and sealed by the court and kept in the custody of the court` MEANS
    IF `the document was obtained pursuant to a warrant, authorization or order issued in accordance with subsection 488.01(3)` OR `the document is the subject of an order made under subsection 488.01(6) or paragraph 488.01(10)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.02(2)
-- jural: a journalist and the relevant media outlet > an officer > right
-- src:9899 | (2) No officer is to examine or reproduce, in whole or in part, a document referred to in subsection (1) without giving the journalist and relevant media outlet notice of his or her intention to examine or reproduce the document.
@ref s 488.02(2) (src:9899)
-- A bar: JUST TRUE where no notice of the intention has been given; once notice is given the bar of this subsection no longer speaks (NOTHING: "without giving ... notice" limits the bar in its own wording).
GIVEN `the document is one referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has given the journalist and the relevant media outlet notice of the intention to examine or reproduce the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.02(2) the officer is barred from examining or reproducing the document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the document is one referred to in subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the officer has given the journalist and the relevant media outlet notice of the intention to examine or reproduce the document` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 488.02(3) who applies` IS ONE OF
    `s 488.02(3) the journalist`
    `s 488.02(3) the relevant media outlet`
    `s 488.02(3) someone else`

-- covers: 488.02(3)
-- fork: F7,G1
-- jural: a journalist or the relevant media outlet > a judge of the court that issued the warrant, authorization or order > power
-- src:9901 | (3) The journalist or relevant media outlet may, within 10 days of receiving the notice referred to in subsection (2), apply to a judge of the court that issued the warrant, authorization or order to issue an order that the document is not to be disclosed to an officer on the grounds that the document identifies or is likely to identity a journalistic source.
@ref s 488.02(3) (src:9901)
-- "within 10 days of receiving the notice": a period fixed in the text's own words, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); fork F7 names the other reading (NOTHING, for a grant).
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 488.02(3) who applies`
      `the application is on the grounds that the document identifies or is likely to identify a journalistic source` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the journalist or media outlet receives the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.02(3) the journalist or media outlet may apply to a judge of the court that issued the warrant, authorization or order for an order that the document is not to be disclosed to an officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF applicant EQUALS `s 488.02(3) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the application is on the grounds that the document identifies or is likely to identify a journalistic source` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the day of the application` GREATER THAN `s 488.02(3) the last day on which the application may be made` `the day the journalist or media outlet receives the notice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 10 days of receiving the notice referred to in subsection (2), apply"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 488.02(3) (the 10 days) (src:9901)
GIVEN `the day the journalist or media outlet receives the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 488.02(3) the last day on which the application may be made` MEANS
    `the day the journalist or media outlet receives the notice` PLUS 10

-- covers: 488.02(4)
-- jural: a journalist > an officer > immunity
