`s 488.02(5) the judge may order the disclosure of the document` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that there is no other way by which the information can reasonably be obtained` AND `the judge is satisfied that the public interest in the investigation and prosecution of a criminal offence outweighs the journalist’s right to privacy in gathering and disseminating information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The judge may order the disclosure of a document only if he or she is satisfied that"

-- covers: 488.02(6)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: the judge > a journalist > power
